    "background_story": "Rowen was a majestic volcano, its conical shape piercing the sky like a shard of stone. Located on a remote island, it stood sentinel over the surrounding landscape, its snow-capped peak glistening in the sunlight. For centuries, Rowen lay dormant, its gentle slopes covered in lush green forests and teeming with wildlife. But when it finally erupted, the explosion was cataclysmic, spewing ash and lava into the atmosphere. The volcano's conical shape funneled the molten rock into a fiery torrent, reshaping the island's terrain in a matter of hours. As the eruption subsided, Rowen's cone was transformed, its symmetrical shape now scarred and rugged. Yet, even in its altered state, the volcano remained a testament to the awe-inspiring power of geological forces.",
